# Settings for this server (PLACEHOLDERS ONLY).
# Railway: scripts/deploy.sh sets the real values as service variables.
# Docker Compose: copy this file to .env (chmod 600) and fill it in: docs/deploy-docker.md.
#   With Compose, a value that contains $ goes in single quotes, e.g. NAME='a$b'.
# Garmin email/password are never stored anywhere: in full mode you log in once,
# interactively, inside the container (docs/garmin-login.md).

# Required: the owner secret you type on the server's sign-in page when Claude
# connects. scripts/deploy.sh generates it on the first run and never prints it.
# See it with: railway variable list --kv | grep ^OWNER_SECRET=
# With Docker Compose: generate it with the command in docs/deploy-docker.md; read it with grep '^OWNER_SECRET=' .env
OWNER_SECRET=generated-at-deploy

# Required: how this server reads Garmin. No default: pick one.
#   full = log in to Garmin once with your email and password (garmin-mcp-auth inside the container). Every tool.
#   key  = a Garmin Personal API key you create in Garmin Connect on the web. Fewer tools: docs/tools.md
#          lists each mode's tools.
GARMIN_AUTH=
# Only with GARMIN_AUTH=key: the key. It is a secret like a password: never commit
# it or paste it elsewhere. Garmin shows it once. Deleting it in Garmin Connect
# stops this server's Garmin access at once. Leave it unset or empty in full mode.
# GARMIN_PERSONAL_API_KEY=

# Optional sign-in settings; leave them unset unless you need them.
# This server's public https origin: for a custom domain on Railway, and always with Docker Compose (the tunnel's hostname):
# PUBLIC_URL=https://coach.example.com
# A static header token for Claude Code or CI (`./scripts/deploy.sh --rotate-token` sets it):
# MCP_BEARER_TOKEN=
# Where the sign-ins are stored (default: on the /data volume):
# AUTH_DB=/data/auth.sqlite
# Extra exact https redirect URIs a client may register, comma-separated (at most 10):
# ALLOWED_REDIRECT_URIS=
# Extra browser origins allowed to call /mcp (comma-separated). This server's own
# origin, https://claude.ai and https://claude.com are always allowed. Use https://
# (http:// only for 127.0.0.1, localhost or [::1] when running locally).
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# off turns the /mcp Origin check off.
# ORIGIN_CHECK=on

# Required: your IANA time zone, e.g. Europe/London. No default: the server does
# not start until it is set. get_daily_status and get_weekly_status use it for
# "today" and "yesterday".
REPORT_TZ=

# Tools: the server exposes only the read-only tools listed in
# config/enabled-tools.txt, which is baked into the image. Write tools cannot be
# enabled here (only PLAN_WRITES below adds the plan's own two). Optional: GARMIN_ENABLED_TOOLS (comma-separated) narrows that list;
# a name that is not in it (a write tool, an unknown name) stops the server at
# startup. In key mode only the tools of config/enabled-tools-key.txt exist.
# GARMIN_ENABLED_TOOLS=get_activities,get_daily_status,get_sleep_summary

# Optional features, both off by default. Leave them unset to keep the server as it is.
# Tracing (docs/tracing.md): traces and metrics, with no health values, to an OTLP/HTTP service.
# TRACING=on
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=https://otlp.example.com/otlp
# The service's auth header, a secret (name=value, comma-separated):
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=
# History search (docs/history-search.md, docs/history-worker.md): Railway only for now. It
# needs an image built with the build argument HISTORY=1, a Postgres with pgvector, and a
# worker service (ROLE=worker); the Docker Compose setup builds without HISTORY=1 and has no
# Postgres, so with Docker leave HISTORY_SEARCH unset (the server would not start).
# HISTORY_SEARCH=on
# The Postgres URL, a secret:
# DATABASE_URL=
# Full mode only, a secret, the same on the app and the worker: 32 random bytes in base64.
# HISTORY_TOKEN_KEY=
# app (default), worker (the job worker) or enqueue (the daily cron run):
# ROLE=app
# Worker threads, 1 to 4 (default 1):
# WORKER_CONCURRENCY=1
# Delete the stored history at the next start, then remove the line again:
# HISTORY_FORGET=yes
# Training plans (docs/training-plan.md): needs HISTORY_SEARCH=on and GARMIN_AUTH=full;
# set it on the app service only. On its own it only previews: nothing is written to Garmin.
# PLAN_TOOLS=on
# Garmin plan writes, off by default (SECURITY.md, "How plan writes behave"): needs
# PLAN_TOOLS=on. Adds plan_commit and plan_cancel, which put a plan's approved days on your
# Garmin calendar and delete them again (only the plan's own workouts). After turning it on,
# reconnect Claude and tick "Also allow this app to change my Garmin calendar" on the
# consent page; older sign-ins keep read access. Turning it off leaves the plan's workouts on your
# calendar: to delete them, run "python ext/launch.py --plan-cleanup" (it works with the switch off too).
# PLAN_WRITES=off
# Plan tracking, log_feedback, plan_activate and plan_review_week (needs PLAN_TOOLS=on): starts
# or stops following a stored plan (plan_activate, also with PLAN_WRITES=off), links activities to
# the active plan's sessions, stores RPE and pain and the weekly review's proposals in the app's own
# database, never in Garmin (with PLAN_WRITES=on too, plan_apply_changes writes approved ones):
# PLAN_TRACKING=on
